    "type": "service",
    "title": "Leaf Chlorophyll Content (Cab)",
    "description": "Calculates the leaf chlorophyll content (Cab, chlorophyll a+b) from Sentinel-2 L2A imagery using the SNAP biophysical neural network ported from SNAP. Cab is expressed in micrograms per square centimetre (\u00b5g/cm\u00b2) and is a key indicator of photosynthetic capacity, nitrogen status and vegetation stress. The neural network takes 8 spectral bands and 4 angular inputs (view and sun geometry) and applies the SNAP BVNet weights, denormalizing to physical units before dividing by 300 to map the 0-300 \u00b5g/cm\u00b2 display range to 0-1. Suitable for crop nitrogen and fertilization management, vegetation stress and disease detection, and phenology monitoring across croplands, forests, and natural ecosystems. Adapted from a SentinelHub Custom Script by Authors not listed.",
